  "notes": "{却下|きゃっか} means to formally reject or dismiss a request, proposal, or legal claim. It implies an authority figure or body making the decision.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{申請|しんせい}→申請：04207_shinsei⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{却下|きゃっか}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to reject an application\n- ⟦{提案|ていあん}→提案：03536_teian⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{却下|きゃっか}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to reject a proposal\n- ⟦{訴|うった}え→訴える：01891_uttaeru⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{却下|きゃっか}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to dismiss a lawsuit\n- ⟦{即座|そくざ}→即座：11861_sokuza⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{却下|きゃっか}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to reject immediately\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{拒否|きょひ}→拒否：08242_kyohi⟧: refusal (broader; can be used for personal refusals)\n- ⟦{棄却|ききゃく}→棄却：05965_kikyaku⟧: dismissal (legal term, more technical; used for court rulings)\n- {不承認|ふしょうにん}: disapproval (bureaucratic, less forceful)\n- ⟦{承認|しょうにん}→承認：03237_shounin⟧: approval (opposite)\n\nREGISTER:\nFormal. Primary domains are legal proceedings, bureaucratic processes, and business decisions. In casual speech, {却下|きゃっか}！ is sometimes used humorously to flatly reject someone's idea or suggestion.",
